# GD-11, C4-1 (round 19, writer 10): L §5.14.2 "It orders a decision only against another decision: plans and
# observations come first, and `before m` with m a plan or an observation is refused (LOAD-ORDER)"; L §8.3 `<a> before
# <m>: <m> is a plan or an observation`. wage is a plan: refused (snap14 read konto before wage). The old comment:
# Fault f_before (writer 6): `before wage` was ignored. L §5.14.2 "A written order outside a cycle": "`before m` may
# also put a decision ahead of a movement it would otherwise follow; the decision then reads the balance before m
# (SF-15)". sweep (a decision reading konto) and the plan wage (1 PLN into konto) fall on 2026-01-15; konto starts at 0
# (its lifespan starts on 2026-01-01). With `before wage`, sweep reads konto before wage: max(0, 0) = 0.00 PLN.
=== f_before.tally
model fbefore
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place save: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

input day: date

move sweep: transfers
  on day
  reads konto
  before wage
  leg cash from konto to save amount max(0, bal(konto))

move wage: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1 PLN

ask q: flows(sweep, 2026-01-15) law 2026-01-31

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  day = 2026-01-15 "row"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-ORDER sweep before wage: wage is a plan or an observation (f_before.tally:19)
